Apple Pie Cyser (Makes One Gallon (Hopefully))

Adapted to One Gallon (Original Recipe: homebrewtalk.com/threads/apple-pie-cyser.436094/)

Ingredients:

1 Gallon Apple Cider
1 Pound Wildflower Honey (13 oz for primary, 3 oz for secondary)
12 oz Brown Sugar
8 oz Apple Juice Concentrate
1 Teaspoon Apple Pie Spice
1 Cinnamon Stick
1/2 Packet Yeast (US-05/S-04)

Procedure:

1. Add 3 qts of cider to 2 gallon fermenting bucket.
2. Add remaining cider to a pot; add spices in a cheesecloth sack to pot before bringing to a simmer. As that heats up, aerate cider in bucket by stirring.
3. Once cider reaches a simmer, remove from heat, take out spice bag, and add 13 oz of the honey and all of the brown sugar. Allow to cool to room temp.
4. Add honey/cider mixture to the bucket and mix well. Pitch yeast.
5. Install airlock; store in a cool, dry place until airlock has less than 1 bubble per minute (original recipe says about 2.5 weeks, but likely longer).
6. Dissolve 3 oz honey into 2 cups warm water. Stir in apple juice concentrate. Add to 1 gallon carboy.
7. Rack over from bucket into carboy. Fine.
8. Allow to clear for 2-3 weeks. Rack into bottles.
9. Age for 6 months.
